---
title: "authorize_upgrade (Sui Framework: package)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_not_pending: assert cap.package != @0x0.to_id()
    q_check_not_pending --> q_abort_pending: cap.package == @0x0
    q_abort_pending --> [*]: abort EAlreadyAuthorized
    q_check_not_pending --> q_check_policy: no pending upgrade
    q_check_policy --> q_abort_policy: policy < cap.policy
    q_abort_policy --> [*]: abort ETooPermissive
    q_check_policy --> q_save_package: policy >= cap.policy
    q_save_package --> q_nullify: package = cap.package
    q_nullify --> q_create_ticket: cap.package = @0x0 (locked)
    q_create_ticket --> [*]: return UpgradeTicket(cap_id, package, policy, digest)

    note right of q_check_not_pending
        INV-001: only one pending upgrade at a time (cap.package set to @0x0)
        INV-002: policy must be at least as restrictive as cap.policy
        INV-003: UpgradeTicket is a hot potato (must be consumed)
        INV-004: digest binds ticket to specific bytecode
    end note
